this CloudCompare link
)

A flat helix (
helicoid
) is a ruled surface, but it is not a developable surface. So you are going to have a flattening problem.

Referring to solid model for geometry not dimensioned is permissible. All unspecified surfaces must match solid model within .020 in. (and we put the .020 in a 
GD&T profile symbol
)

I use CAD Assistant(
https://www.opencascade.com/products/cad-assistant/
) to convert STEP files into GLTF, and from there import the GLTF files into Blender for further processing and exporting to Collada and STL.
